.TH DOT-THEME 1 "August 2026" "dotfiles v0.2.503" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dot\-theme \- switch terminal + desktop theme across families and modes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dot theme
.RI [ subcommand ]
.RI [ arguments ]
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dot theme
is the wallpaper\-driven theming system for the dotfiles framework.
Each theme bundles a wallpaper family (dark + light variants), a
terminal palette, GTK/icon/cursor themes, an accent colour, and font
choices, all derived from the wallpaper's dominant colours by
.BR extract\-theme (7).
Applying a theme regenerates configs via
.BR chezmoi (1)
and signals every running application to reload.
.PP
The dispatcher detects the running desktop (GNOME family via
.IR gsettings ,
KDE Plasma via
.IR plasma\-apply\-* / kwriteconfig6 ,
XFCE via
.IR xfconf\-query ,
wlroots via
.IR swww / hyprctl )
and routes writes to the correct backend.
On macOS the applier speaks
.IR osascript " and " defaults
directly.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.SS Discovery
.TP
.B list
Show every paired wallpaper theme.
.TP
.B current
Print the active theme name.
.TP
.B status \fR[\fB\-\-json\fR]
Diagnostic dashboard: recorded theme vs.
live
.IR gsettings / kwriteconfig
state, detected DE, wallpaper URIs.
.TP
.B diff \fITHEME_A\fR \fITHEME_B\fR
Side\-by\-side field diff (family, mode, accent, wallpaper, bg, fg)
with 24\-bit ANSI colour swatches; rows that differ are marked
.RB \(dq \(!= \(dq.
.SS Selection
.TP
.B set \fITHEME\fR \fR[\fB\-\-force\fR|\fB\-\-full\fR|\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR]
Apply a named theme. Idempotent no\-op when the target is already
active. Pass
.B \-\-force
to re\-apply anyway (useful after editing config templates),
.B \-\-full
to run the full
.B chezmoi apply
instead of the targeted 12\-template subset, or
.B \-\-dry\-run
to print what would happen without touching anything.
.TP
.B toggle
Flip light \(-> dark within the current family.
.TP
.B mode \fR{\fBdark\fR|\fBlight\fR|\fBauto\fR}
Idempotently force a mode.
.B auto
is an alias for
.BR sync .
.TP
.B family
Cycle to the next paired family, preserving mode.
.TP
.B random \fR[\fB\-\-mode\fR \fIdark\fR|\fIlight\fR]
Pick a random family. Preserves current mode unless overridden.
.TP
.B preview \fITHEME\fR
Apply the theme, then block waiting for
.B ENTER
(keep) or
.B Ctrl\-C
(revert to previous).
.SS Live tweaks (no theme change)
.TP
.B accent \fR[\fICOLOR\fR|\fIINT\fR]
Set only the desktop accent. Accepts a GNOME accent enum name
(blue, teal, green, yellow, orange, red, pink, purple, slate) or an
integer on the
.I macos_accent
scale (\-1 = slate, 0\-6 = red\-pink).
No arg = show current.
.TP
.B wallpaper \fR[\fIPATH\fR]
Set an arbitrary wallpaper without a theme swap.
.TP
.B fit \fIMODE\fR
Wallpaper scale mode: zoom, spanned, centered, scaled, stretched,
wallpaper (tiled), none.
.SS History
.TP
.B undo
Step back to the previous theme. Toggle behaviour: rerun to bounce
back and forth.
.TP
.B history
Print the recently\-applied stack (up to 20 entries, newest first).
.SS Portability
.TP
.B export \fR[\fIFILE\fR]
Snapshot current theme + fit to JSON.
.I FILE
missing or
.B \-
means stdout.
.TP
.B import \fIFILE\fR
Restore theme + fit from a snapshot. Verifies the target theme
exists in
.I themes.toml
first — an error, not a silent misapply, if the target machine
hasn't run
.B rebuild
yet.
.SS Sync + Automation
.TP
.B sync
Match the theme to the system's dark/light preference
.RB ( gsettings " " color\-scheme " on GNOME, " kdeglobals " ColorScheme on KDE)."
.TP
.B ambient \fR{\fBrun\fR|\fBenable\fR|\fBdisable\fR|\fBstatus\fR}
Time\-of\-day auto\-switch. Sunrise/sunset resolves via env vars,
.BR sunwait (1)
with
.BR DOT_THEME_LOCATION ,
a state file, then fixed 07:00 / 19:00.
.B enable
installs a systemd user timer (hourly + on login,
.BR Persistent=true ).
.TP
.B rotate \fR{\fBenable\fR \fR[\fIINTERVAL\fR]\fR|\fBdisable\fR|\fBstatus\fR}
Periodic random\-family wallpaper rotator via systemd user timer.
Default 30m interval. Runs alongside
.B ambient
cleanly — ambient handles mode, rotate handles family.
.SS Maintenance
.TP
.B reset
Restore GNOME defaults (accent, cursor, fonts, shell\-theme).
Wallpaper is deliberately not cleared.
.TP
.B help
Print the built\-in usage listing (mirrors this SUBCOMMANDS section).
.TP
.B rebuild \fR[\fB\-\-force\fR|\fB\-\-list\fR]
Regenerate
.I themes.toml
by scanning wallpaper directories and running
.BR extract\-theme (7)
on each. Runs
.BR extract\-heic\-frames.sh (7)
first on Linux so paired PNGs exist for every dynamic HEIC before
theme discovery.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DOT_THEME_CURSOR_DARK\fR, \fBDOT_THEME_CURSOR_LIGHT
Override the mode\-linked cursor theme
(defaults: Bibata\-Modern\-Classic / \-Ice).
.TP
.B DOT_THEME_MONO_FONT\fR, \fBDOT_THEME_UI_FONT\fR, \fBDOT_THEME_DOC_FONT
Override fonts per slot. Falls through to \(dqdon't touch\(dq if
neither the theme nor the env var sets it.
.TP
.B DOT_THEME_GNOME_SHELL
Override the GNOME Shell theme name
.RB ( org.gnome.shell.extensions.user\-theme "  ).
Falls back to matching the GTK theme name when a
.I /gnome\-shell
directory exists under
.IR /usr/share/themes , " ~/.themes" ", or "  ~/.local/share/themes .
.TP
.B DOT_THEME_SUNRISE\fR, \fBDOT_THEME_SUNSET
Fixed times for the
.B ambient
switcher (HH:MM).
.TP
.B DOT_THEME_LOCATION
lat,lon pair for
.BR sunwait (1)
lookup, e.g.
.RB \(dq 51.5N,0.13W \(dq.
.TP
.B DOT_THEME_SEQUENTIAL
Set to
.B 1
to force the reload chain to run sequentially instead of in
parallel. Useful for reproducing per\-step timing bugs.
.TP
.B DOTFILES_WALLPAPER_DIR
Override the wallpaper library location
.RB (default: ~/Pictures/Wallpapers ).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/dot/theme\-history
Persistent history stack for
.BR undo .
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/dot/theme\-ambient.conf
Persistent sunrise/sunset config for
.BR ambient .
.TP
.I ~/.config/systemd/user/dot\-theme\-ambient.{service,timer}
Ambient timer unit files installed by
.BR "ambient enable" .
.TP
.I ~/.config/systemd/user/dot\-theme\-rotate.{service,timer}
Rotate timer unit files installed by
.BR "rotate enable" .
.TP
.I ${DOTFILES}/defaults/.chezmoidata/themes.toml
The generated theme catalogue read by every apply.
.TP
.I ${DOTFILES}/defaults/.chezmoidata.toml
Records the currently\-active theme via a
.B theme
key.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Interactive picker with palette preview:
.PP
.RS
.B dot theme
.RE
.PP
Random dark family, keep applying every 15 minutes:
.PP
.RS
.B dot theme rotate enable 15m
.RE
.PP
Try a theme, decide with the keyboard:
.PP
.RS
.B dot theme preview Firewatch\-dark
.RE
.PP
Snapshot the current setup and restore it on another machine:
.PP
.RS
.B "dot theme export ~/theme\-snap.json"
.br
.B "scp ~/theme\-snap.json new\-box:"
.br
.B "ssh new\-box 'dot theme import ~/theme\-snap.json'"
.RE
.PP
Sun\-based auto light/dark in London:
.PP
.RS
.B "DOT_THEME_LOCATION=\(dq51.5N,0.13W\(dq dot theme ambient enable"
.RE
.PP
Diagnostic sweep (all live vs recorded state):
.PP
.RS
.B "dot theme status \-\-json | jq"
.RE
.SH PERFORMANCE
.PP
On a modern workstation, an idempotent no\-op set completes in
about 40 ms; a full apply with the parallel reload chain in about
550 ms (chezmoi\-dominated). Setting
.B DOT_THEME_SEQUENTIAL=1
adds roughly 30 % to that.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dot (1),
.BR chezmoi (1),
.BR sunwait (1),
.BR gsettings (1),
.BR kwriteconfig6 (1),
.BR xfconf\-query (1)
